{% doc %}
  A tab strip and its panels.

  Generic on purpose. The mega menu is the first caller, but nothing here knows
  about navigation — a product page, a size guide or a comparison table can
  render the same shell and get the same keyboard behaviour and the same sliding
  marker for free.

  ## The caller builds the tabs and panels

  Passing captured strings rather than a list of objects is how `carousel-shell`
  works in this theme, and for the same reason: the caller already has the loop,
  the ids and the content, and rebuilding all three inside a snippet means every
  new use has to bend its data into a shape the snippet invented.

  Each tab must be a `<button role="tab">` carrying `id`, `aria-controls`,
  `aria-selected` and `tabindex`, and each panel a `role="tabpanel"` carrying
  `id` and `aria-labelledby`. The first tab is the selected one; every other
  panel is `hidden`.

  ## The marker

  One absolutely positioned element that moves, rather than a background on the
  active tab that switches instantly. It is inside the tablist and
  `aria-hidden`, so it is decoration to assistive technology and geometry to the
  browser.

  @param {string} tabs - The `role="tab"` buttons
  @param {string} panels - The `role="tabpanel"` elements
  @param {string} [orientation] - horizontal | vertical. Default: horizontal
  @param {string} [activation] - auto | manual. Default: auto
  @param {boolean} [hover] - Select on pointer hover as well as click
  @param {string} [label] - Accessible name for the tablist
  @param {string} [classes]

  @example
    {% render 'tab-group', tabs: tabs, panels: panels, orientation: 'vertical' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign tab_orientation = orientation | default: 'horizontal'
  assign tab_activation = activation | default: 'auto'
-%}

<tab-group
  class="tabs tabs--{{ tab_orientation }} {{ classes }}"
  data-orientation="{{ tab_orientation }}"
  data-activation="{{ tab_activation }}"
  {% if hover %}data-hover="true"{% endif %}
>
  <div class="tabs__rail">
    <div
      class="tabs__list"
      role="tablist"
      aria-orientation="{{ tab_orientation }}"
      {% if label != blank %}aria-label="{{ label | escape }}"{% endif %}
      data-ref="list"
    >
      <span class="tabs__marker" data-ref="marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {{ tabs }}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="tabs__panels" data-ref="panels">
    {{ panels }}
  </div>
</tab-group>
